		<div style="font-size:13px;display:block;margin-block-end:13px;margin-block-start:13px;margin-inline-end:0px;margin-inline-start:0px;">The fact that you can ping "b" from "a" does not imply that TCP (and thus simpletun) works at all. You must make sure you have TCP access from "a" to "b" on the port used by simpletun (55555 by default, can be changed with -p).</div>

		
