		<div style="font-size:13px;display:block;margin-block-end:13px;margin-block-start:13px;margin-inline-end:0px;margin-inline-start:0px;">The tun interface is just another interface. In your testcase, if you had eth5 instead of the tun interface, nothing would change.<br>
If a packet enters eth0 and iptables drops all packets entering eth0, they will be dropped and thus will not reach eth5, or tun0, or whatever other interface.<br>
If a packet enters eth1 and it is down, it is dropped even before iptables has a word on it.<br>
In short, iptables-wise there's no difference between a tun interface and another physical interface.</div>

		
