		<div style="font-size:13px;display:block;margin-block-end:13px;margin-block-start:13px;margin-inline-end:0px;margin-inline-start:0px;">What I like is a minimal design, and a bridge doesn't need a MAC address.  I understand that a Linux box might offer more than a regular switch, and for that you need a MAC address.  But the services should be provided by a new tap interface added to the bridge.  I believe that the bridge should not even be shown by ifconfig.</div>
<div style="font-size:13px;display:block;margin-block-end:13px;margin-block-start:13px;margin-inline-end:0px;margin-inline-start:0px;">That's interesting that the bridge takes the lowest MAC address of the bridge interfaces.  I wonder why this is needed.</div>

		
