<div style="font-size:13px;display:block;margin-block-end:13px;margin-block-start:13px;margin-inline-end:0px;margin-inline-start:0px;">Finally, I was able to get the program working again if:<br>
   ifconfig tap0 down<br>
   ifconfig tap1 down<br>
   rmmod -f tun<br>
   modprobe tun</div>
<div style="font-size:13px;display:block;margin-block-end:13px;margin-block-start:13px;margin-inline-end:0px;margin-inline-start:0px;">Then it works again...</div>
<div style="font-size:13px;display:block;margin-block-end:13px;margin-block-start:13px;margin-inline-end:0px;margin-inline-start:0px;">I discovered that I can create the tap devices using iproute2, and then connect to them later on in my program.  Then, I simply leave the tap devices created always and I they persist after my program exits.  Would this be a better way of doing this?</div>
